            <div xml:id="d816">

                <pb facs="0941" n="845" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg845"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.516/39: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Salvador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Arnold</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-06-25T18:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 25, 1921—6
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received June 26—8:10
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>26. Concession signed and approved by National Assembly to René Keilhauer for the
                    establishment of last [<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>] bank of emission,
                    authorized capital $10,000,000, gold guarantee for bills will be deposited in
                    banks in the United States. Cabinet has approved 60-day option to René Keilhauer
                    for $16,000,000 loan to be guaranteed by customs receipts and customhouses to be
                    controlled by two controllers, one named by bankers and other by Government, all
                    differences to be submitted to Chief Justice of the United States as
                    arbitrator.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Arnold</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
